        "original_id": "be9075cb-84f5-513c-9288-0882df76d98d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Na Fianna Éireann, British House of Commons, Dáil Éireann, Sinn Féin, Fianna Fáil\n- People: Constance Markievicz, Bulmer Hobson\n- Roles: Irish nationalist youth organisation, politician, revolutionary nationalist, suffragette, socialist\n\nFacts:\n- Na Fianna Éireann, also known as the Fianna, is an Irish nationalist youth organisation founded in 1909 by Bulmer Hobson and Constance Markievicz.\n- Constance Georgine Markievicz, also known as Countess Markievicz and née Gore-Booth, was born on 4 February 1868 and died on 15 July 1927.\n- Constance Markievicz was an Irish Sinn Féin and Fianna Fáil politician, revolutionary nationalist, suffragette, and socialist.\n- In December 1918, Constance Markievicz became the first woman elected to the British House of Commons.\n- Constance Markievicz did not take her seat in the British House of Commons and, with the other Sinn Féin TDs, formed the first Dáil Éireann.",
